# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-serve-4 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-4 throughout: B4 builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after B4's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# F1 (the T5b arm): the T1-only arm of the audit factorial, c2-packed-tp4-diag-t1 (the verify T1 shard-argmax audit on, T2 off), with the
# instruments (stage markers, collectives log, L1 view, the census with its graph part EXPLICITLY off), the stall watch and the handle
# guard in log mode. The old tail narrowing (caps off) reproduces the packed-to-sequential transition that hung. Run it only if FX
# stalls or the hang is not yet localised. The same tests as the last window's diagnosis; each run either stalls (the stall watch dumps
# every thread, runs the triage tools, then ends the process) or completes.
# Reading: T1-only completes and T2-only stalls points to the T1 audit's effect inside the packed capture (the CCL handle count, or the
# pinned sampler moving before capture); T2-only completes and T1-only stalls points to the packed capture's freed temporaries; both
# complete or both stall gives no reading. A single completion is weak evidence.
# Duration (estimate): 20 min. Not a stop job.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-4
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-diag-t1
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4_v164order,concurrent4_steady,replay_concurrent4
